  "question": {
    "text": "The temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> moles of a gas at constant volume is changed from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The change in internal energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The total heat capacity of the gas at constant volume (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) is"
  },
